    💭 GET and HEAD
    🧪🐇🔬🔸🧭 app 🔤GET🔤 🔤/inspect?x=1&x=2🔤❗️ ➡️ get
    🔢 check 🔤GET is served🔤 🚥 get❗️ 200❗️
    🔍 check 🔤GET reaches the handler with its method🔤 📄 get❗️ 🔤method=GET❌n🔤❗️
    🔍 check 🔤GET reaches the handler with its query🔤 📄 get❗️ 🔤query.x=1❌nquery.x=2❌n🔤❗️
    🧪🐇🔬🔸🧭 app 🔤HEAD🔤 🔤/🔤❗️ ➡️ head
    🔢 check 🔤HEAD is answered from the GET route🔤 🚥 head❗️ 200❗️
    🔡 check 🔤HEAD has no body🔤 📄 head❗️ 🔤🔤❗️
    🔡 check 🔤HEAD keeps the length the GET body has🔤 🏷🐇🔬🔸🧭 head 🔤Content-Length🔤❗️ 🔤2🔤❗️
    🔡 check 🔤HEAD keeps the content type🔤 🏷🐇🔬🔸🧭 head 🔤Content-Type🔤❗️ 🔤text/plain; charset=utf-8🔤❗️
    🧪🐇🔬🔸🧭 app 🔤HEAD🔤 🔤/inspect/abc🔤❗️ ➡️ headParam
    🔢 check 🔤HEAD works on a route with a parameter🔤 🚥 headParam❗️ 200❗️
    🔡 check 🔤and still has no body🔤 📄 headParam❗️ 🔤🔤❗️
    🧪🐇🔬🔸🧭 app 🔤HEAD🔤 🔤/stream/3🔤❗️ ➡️ headStream
    🔢 check 🔤HEAD on a streamed route is 200🔤 🚥 headStream❗️ 200❗️
    🔡 check 🔤HEAD on a streamed route has no body🔤 📄 headStream❗️ 🔤🔤❗️
    🔡 check 🔤HEAD on a streamed route claims no length🔤 🏷🐇🔬🔸🧭 headStream 🔤Content-Length🔤❗️ 🔤(none)🔤❗️
    🧪🐇🔬🔸🧭 app 🔤HEAD🔤 🔤/bytes🔤❗️ ➡️ headPost
